  "goodToKnow": "Das Sägewerk is a sawmill, where logs (Baumstämme) are cut into boards (Bretter) and beams (Balken). Germany's forests, such as the Black Forest, have many, and historic water-powered ones are museums. Die Säge is a saw; sägen means to saw and colloquially to snore. Das Werk means works or plant. Plural: die Sägewerke."
